# Each destination below is its own separately-deployed Netlify site. These
# rules proxy that content through the main domain at a clean path --
# status 200 means "rewrite", so the address bar keeps showing
# noblefathercreations.com/<slug> instead of jumping to *.netlify.app.
#
# NOTE: an exact-match source (no `*`) must NOT use :splat in its
# destination -- there is no wildcard to capture, and Netlify accepts the
# syntax while the rule then fails to serve. Only the paired /slug/* rule
# gets :splat.

# ---- the library (books) ----
/feminine      https://sovereign-woman.netlify.app/                  200
/feminine/*    https://sovereign-woman.netlify.app/:splat            200
/children      https://playgroundprotector.netlify.app/              200
/children/*    https://playgroundprotector.netlify.app/:splat        200
/wook          https://wook-in-sheeps-clothing.netlify.app/          200
/wook/*        https://wook-in-sheeps-clothing.netlify.app/:splat    200
/fractal       https://thefractal.netlify.app/                       200
/fractal/*     https://thefractal.netlify.app/:splat                 200
/fracture      https://fractures.netlify.app/                        200
/fracture/*    https://fractures.netlify.app/:splat                  200
/faith         https://thenobledivide.netlify.app/                   200
/faith/*       https://thenobledivide.netlify.app/:splat             200
/loop          https://noble-the-loop.netlify.app/                   200
/loop/*        https://noble-the-loop.netlify.app/:splat             200
/scale         https://noble-the-weighing.netlify.app/               200
/scale/*       https://noble-the-weighing.netlify.app/:splat         200

# ---- the lab (tools + music) ----
/playbook      https://noblepatterns.netlify.app/                    200
/playbook/*    https://noblepatterns.netlify.app/:splat              200
/shadowroot    https://nobleshadows.netlify.app/                     200
/shadowroot/*  https://nobleshadows.netlify.app/:splat               200
/music         https://noblemusic.netlify.app/                       200
/music/*       https://noblemusic.netlify.app/:splat                 200

# ---- the workshop (craft) ----
/portals       https://nfcportals.netlify.app/                       200
/portals/*     https://nfcportals.netlify.app/:splat                 200
/press         https://noblenfcseals.netlify.app/                    200
/press/*       https://noblenfcseals.netlify.app/:splat              200
/resin         https://incandescent-kataifi-cde77d.netlify.app/      200
/resin/*       https://incandescent-kataifi-cde77d.netlify.app/:splat 200

# The Casting is the ONLY multi-file project in the catalogue -- every book
# is a single self-contained HTML file, so proxying them at /slug just
# works. The Casting is a real static site whose CSS, JS, images and JSON
# are separate files referenced with ROOT-relative paths (/assets/…,
# /data/…) -- see its own DEPLOYING.md, which warns that the site assumes
# it lives at a domain root. Proxied at /resin, the browser still asks
# THIS domain for /assets/css/theme.css, which 404s here, so the whole
# gallery rendered as unstyled text with no photos and no data.
#
# These two rules hand those prefixes to The Casting. Safe because the hub
# deploy is a single index.html and owns nothing under /assets or /data,
# and because Netlify serves a real file in preference to a rewrite -- so
# if the hub ever does ship its own /assets, that wins automatically.
# If a SECOND multi-file project is ever added, these must be namespaced
# (and that project's asset paths made relative) rather than duplicated.
# EVERY top-level path The Casting owns has to be listed here, not just its
# assets. Missing /statues is what made "View the Collection" and every
# individual piece 404 even after the styling was fixed: those links are
# root-relative too, so they resolved against THIS domain. The full set is
# /assets, /data and /statues -- if the Casting ever adds another top-level
# directory, it must be added here in the same breath or its links break the
# same way. `npm run verify` (scripts/verify-live.mjs) crawls every internal
# link on every page and fails on any 404, which is the guard against this.
/assets/*      https://incandescent-kataifi-cde77d.netlify.app/assets/:splat 200
/data/*        https://incandescent-kataifi-cde77d.netlify.app/data/:splat   200
/statues       https://incandescent-kataifi-cde77d.netlify.app/statues       200
/statues/*     https://incandescent-kataifi-cde77d.netlify.app/statues/:splat 200

# Singular/alternate spellings people are likely to type or to have been
# given on a card, kept as real redirects (301) so there is one canonical
# path per product rather than two addresses serving identical content.
/portal        /portals                                              301
/seals         /press                                                301

/festival      https://noble-festie-bible.netlify.app/                200
/festival/*    https://noble-festie-bible.netlify.app/:splat          200
